  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the white man in prayer",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the visual material of the white man praying with a rosary, as this image is central to the meme's hateful framing. The user is implicitly positioned as the 'observer' or 'questioner' of the narrative presented in the text, which asks 'how black people became christians.' The visual of the white man in prayer is used to represent the 'proper' or 'authentic' form of Christian practice, and the user is projected onto this visual as the one who is 'asking' or 'thinking' the question implied by the text. This projection reinforces the racialized hierarchy by equating the user's perspective with the white, Catholic, passive form of Christianity depicted in the image.",
